--
--
Instantiating vector<pair<T,U>>::emplace_back with a
non-default-constructible T hard-fails a constrained pair constructor
instead of discarding it ([temp.deduct]/8).  Root ingredient of the
sharing_node pair<ssa_exprt,...> failures in the goto_symex_state and
abstract_environment dog-food TUs.
Diagnosis 2026-07-23: during emplace_back's instantiation, pair's
SFINAE-constrained default constructor instance (stl_pair.h:544,
gated on is_default_constructible) is eagerly converted although
never odr-used ([temp.inst]/4,/11); its mem-initializer `first()`
finds no symbolish ctor.  The nested failure is swallowed per
function, but emplace_back's own candidate is lost and the
[temp.deduct]/8 all-templates-failed path escalates via
pending_no_viable_call at depth 0.  push_back with an explicit pair
WORKS -- only the member-template instantiation path is affected.
Update 2026-07-24 (mechanism pinned): the candidate SIGNATURE is
formed with the pack homogenised -- pack_deduced_types deduces
{symbolish, unsigned long} correctly, but the function-type expansion
of `_Args&&...` consults pack_args_map, which is only recorded AFTER
the type is formed (the late recording serves the return-type path),
so the scalar type_map entry (first element) fills every copy:
emplace_back's own signature becomes (symbolish&&, symbolish&&) and
2ul cannot bind.  Recording the pack EARLY fixes this test but
double-expands two-pack constructors (cpp17_tuple_get_two_pack_ctor_
3elem): the parameter synthesis writes concrete types positionally
AND the typecheck-time pack expansion duplicates them.  The proper
fix is a single expansion point for deduced parameter packs.
